<%- include('/partials/head') %>

<div class="wrap page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Wear More. Waste Less.</p>
  <h1>About ReWear</h1>
  <p class="lede">ReWear is a community clothing reuse platform built as a Community Engagement
    Project. It is deliberately small, practical and local.</p>
</div>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="dash-grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem">The problem we started from</h2>
        <p class="soft">Almost everyone owns clothes bought for one occasion and worn once: a wedding
          outfit, a festival saree, a blazer for an interview, something for a college event. They are
          expensive, they take up space, and they sit unused.</p>
        <p class="soft">Meanwhile the next person who needs that exact outfit for that exact occasion
          usually buys a new one. Within a college or a neighbourhood, those two people are often a
          ten-minute walk apart.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-top:26px">What ReWear does</h2>
        <p class="soft">ReWear lets people in one local community rent clothes to each other, with
          resale and donation as supporting options for items someone is ready to let go of entirely.
          Renting is the main focus: it is the case where one garment can serve many people.</p>
        <p class="soft">The hard part is not listing clothes &mdash; it is trust. So the platform puts
          most of its effort there: verified members, documented condition before and after every
          rental, reviews only after completed transactions, local handover, and minimal personal
          information on display.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="stack">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>What is built and working</h3>
          <ul class="trust">
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Accounts, login and admin verification</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Listings for rent, sale and donation, with photo uploads</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Search, filters and availability by date</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Full rental flow with owner approval</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Condition records before and after, with photos</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Reviews, notifications and reports</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Resale and donation enquiry flow, donation drives</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Community survey and impact dashboard</span></li>
            <li><span class="tick">&#10003;</span><span>Admin dashboard for members, listings and reports</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>What it intentionally does not do</h3>
          <p class="soft" style="margin:0">No payment processing, no delivery network, no insurance, no
            AI. Rent and deposits are settled directly between members. Every one of those would add
            a lot of machinery and very little to the core idea at this scale.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ---------- future scope ---------- -->
<section class="band" id="future">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center" style="max-width:58ch;margin:0 auto 34px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Future scope</p>
      <h2>Where this could go next</h2>
      <p class="soft">None of the following is part of the current version. They are listed as an
        honest roadmap rather than features implied by buttons that do nothing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>Your Digital Wardrobe</h3>
        <p class="soft">Upload your wardrobe and discover ways to rent, resell, donate or style what
          you already own.</p>
        <button class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" type="button" disabled>Coming Soon</button>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>ReWear Score</h3>
        <p class="soft">A reuse score built from rentals, number of wears, resale, donations and item
          condition &mdash; a real calculation over real activity, not a guessed number.</p>
        <button class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" type="button" disabled>Coming Soon</button>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h3>Smarter discovery</h3>
        <p class="soft">Outfit recommendations, size matching from saved measurements, and a proper
          recommendation engine once there is enough activity to learn from.</p>
        <button class="btn btn-quiet btn-sm" type="button" disabled>Coming Soon</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel mt">
      <h3>Longer-term ideas</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <ul class="trust">
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>AI-assisted condition checks from photos</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Digital payments and escrow for deposits</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Delivery and pickup partnerships</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Damage protection or insurance</span></li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="trust">
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Laundry and dry-cleaning partners between rentals</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Verified NGO partnerships for donations</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Community rewards for consistent lenders</span></li>
          <li><span class="tick">&rarr;</span><span>Campus-level and society-level sub-communities</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ---------- CTA ---------- -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band">
      <h2>Have clothes sitting unused?</h2>
      <p>Listing takes about two minutes. Rent them out, resell them, or pass them on.</p>
      <div class="row">
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="<%= user ? '/items/new' : '/register' %>">Give Them Another Life</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" style="border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.55);color:#fff"
           href="/community/survey">Take the survey</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('/partials/foot') %>
